{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1792555633,"nonce":"YDXRXs1Sa/4+rn8FSR9WhTWm488=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"LE_lADOUJip488AAAABYuT_-c8AAAAH3zlVkg","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"assignee:guilbep"},"added":["assignee:guilbep"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1792555633,"nonce":"HNNGqKCJIjzbyCS366Wzuz3FMNk=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"LE_lADOUJip488AAAABYuT_-c8AAAAH3zlWXw","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"assignee:guilbep\nstatus:backlog"},"added":["status:backlog"],"removed":[]},{"type":6,"timestamp":1792556064,"nonce":"dpG+JcOv3s7G7gPVkmHaUy9fFZg=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"UCE_lAHOUJip488AAAABYuT_-c8AAAABDfbh4g","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:text":"16cc7ce78bdca0db2ae1188332f93e42bd319e3643fd0a04a2c9cb72355a7c80"},"target":"c703d866af5186959011f9cada386c0cdf632c8953185ea82866009ab193434d","message":"The fork's `native-fields` build turns kinds into GitHub issue types where EPFL-ENAC has one, and keeps them as labels otherwise. This is what the build needs from you, as an org owner or with one. The decision doc is `doc/design/bridges/native-fields.md` on the fork's local `native-fields` branch, which isn't pushed.\n\n## 1. Issue types in EPFL-ENAC\n\nSettings › Planning › Issue types › Create new type. All six are optional: until a type exists, its kind stays a label on GitHub, and nothing breaks. Each type shows in the type picker of every EPFL-ENAC repository (31 use types today), so it's the organization's call. With all six, the org has 9 of the 25 types allowed.\n\n- [ ] **Polish**: A small improvement to something that works\n- [ ] **Performance**: Faster or lighter, same behaviour\n- [ ] **Refactor**: A code change with no change in behaviour\n- [ ] **Documentation**: Docs only\n- [ ] **Style**: Formatting only\n- [ ] **Test**: Tests only\n\nAlready there: **Bug**, **Feature** and **Task**. Task has no git-board kind, so it comes in as `kind:task`.\n\nco2's kinds are flat labels, so once the types exist its bridges need:\n\n```\nkind-types = bug=Bug,feat=Feature,polish=Polish,perf=Performance,refactor=Refactor,docs=Documentation,style=Style,test=Test\n```\n\ngit-board can't write that key yet: its config doesn't hold each kind's type name (feat is Feature). That's a git-board follow-up. Until then, set the key by hand in each clone that syncs: `git config git-bug.bridge.\u003cname\u003e.kind-types …`.\n\nOn a flat project like co2, a kind must be in the key **before** its type is used. Otherwise an issue typed Polish comes in as `kind:polish` beside `polish`.\n\n## 2. The Priority issue field\n\nEPFL-ENAC already has organization issue fields: **Priority** (Urgent, High, Medium, Low), **Effort** (High, Medium, Low), **Start date** and **Target date**.\n\n- [ ] Check that Priority's four options fit `prio:p0`–`p3` (p0 = Urgent, p1 = High, p2 = Medium, p3 = Low). Complete it if you want other names or descriptions.\n- [ ] Decide whether `prio:` should become that field natively, like kinds. It would be a later build, not part of `native-fields`.\n\n## 3. A scratch repository for the live test\n\n- [ ] A **private** repository in EPFL-ENAC, for example `EPFL-ENAC/git-bug-native-fields-test`\n- [ ] guilbep has write access to it\n- [ ] The token the bridge uses can reach it. A fine-grained token needs the repository, Issues read and write, Metadata read, and an admin's approval if the org asks for one; a classic token needs `repo`.\n- [ ] It stays out of Project 40 and its automation\n\n## Facts behind it (checked 2026-10-21)\n\n- A user-owned repository has no issue types: `guilbep/git-bug-sync-test` answers `issueTypes: null`. So the live test needs an organization repository.\n- EPFL-ENAC has 542 typed issues in 31 repositories; 65 are in co2-calculator (28 Bug, 33 Feature, 4 Task).\n- gitlab.epfl.ch (19.4.2, free edition) has milestones but no iterations. Sprints become existing milestones there; nothing to add.\n\nDone when the types you want exist, the Priority decision is written here, and the scratch repository exists. Then the `native-fields` session runs the live test.","files":null},{"type":8,"timestamp":1792575267,"nonce":"MVIwndsc8SSTroVcp1+2GJcCQfE=","target":"944fb0f297c80e0d509cca4febadee0b1046bcebcfb8263aed079821f1910b78","new_metadata":{"sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"status:backlog"}}]}